{
  "answer": "BianLian group actors are reported using Rclone. [E6, E7, E8, E9]\nLockBit 3.0 actors are reported using Rclone. [E2]\nCISA reports BianLian group actors using Rclone to exfiltrate data to a cloud account they control on the same service to avoid typical file transfers/downloads and network-based exfiltration detection. [E16]\nThe BianLian group uses File Transfer Protocol (FTP) and Rclone to exfiltrate data. [E9]\nUser Account Management (M1018) can mitigate Transfer Data to Cloud Account (T1537). [E10, E11]\nFilter Network Traffic (M1037) can mitigate Transfer Data to Cloud Account (T1537) by implementing network-based filtering restrictions to prohibit data transfers to untrusted VPCs. [E12, E13]\nSoftware Configuration (M1054) can mitigate Transfer Data to Cloud Account (T1537) by configuring appropriate data sharing restrictions in cloud services. [E14, E15]",
